is the same in both directions. Positions are valid until the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is mutated.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counting."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Neighborhoods count edge ends. A vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"w ≠ v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appears in ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once per edge between them. A self-loop has both its ends at ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appears in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" twice per loop, and the loop’s position twice in ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjacency_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", LEMON, igraph). ","type":"text"},{"code":"degree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the length of either, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop counts 2 and the degrees sum to ","type":"text"},{"code":"2 * edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex and edge indices."}]},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": with "},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps the vertices one-to-one onto "},{"code":"0..<vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives adjacency in index space. A representation with dense edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices also reports "},{"code":"edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and then "},{"code":"edgeIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps edge positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-to-one onto "},{"code":"0..<edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"code":"edge_index","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", petgraph’s "},{"code":"EdgeIndexable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms that mark edges (bridges, cut vertices, Euler tours) keep that state in arrays too."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them parallel to "},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every conformer satisfies:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount == vertices.count"},{"text":", the vertices are distinct, and every edge’s endpoints are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount == edges.count"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For every vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the position of each edge with an end at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once per end (a self-loop twice); each such edge has ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as an endpoint;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"oppositeVertex(to: v, acrossEdgeAt: e)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[e].oppositeVertex(to: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighbors(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the opposite vertices in the same order; ","type":"text"},{"code":"degree(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"count.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The degrees sum to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2 * edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", in either orientation, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains"},{"type":"text","text":" is false (and does not trap) for anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absent."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Asking again gives the same answer."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" is in index order: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atIndex: i)"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":"th vertex.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With vertex indices, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: vertexIndex(of: v))"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mapped through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With vertex indices, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges